From: ARM64 enablement — fix KSEG0_BASE for ARM64 kernel VA layout

The previous value (0xfffff80000000000) was the AMD64 KSEG0 base
mistakenly carried over to the ARM64 NDK header. Windows ARM64 uses
the TTBR1_EL1 region starting at 0xFFFF800000000000 (48-bit kernel
VA split). Verified against Win11 ARM64 ntkrnlmp PDB symbols and
absolute references in disassembled scheduler/HAL code.

This is a one-line constant correction with no struct-layout impact
and no ABI surface change.

---
 sdk/include/ndk/arm64/ketypes.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sdk/include/ndk/arm64/ketypes.h b/sdk/include/ndk/arm64/ketypes.h
--- a/sdk/include/ndk/arm64/ketypes.h
+++ b/sdk/include/ndk/arm64/ketypes.h
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
 //
 // Static Kernel-Mode Address start (use MM_KSEG0_BASE for actual)
 //
-#define KSEG0_BASE 0xfffff80000000000ULL
+#define KSEG0_BASE 0xFFFF800000000000ULL

 //
 // Structure for CPUID info
